TorchSpec patches for vllm nightly-7794b1e08bf505ff28664515ffaaeeec955ab796
(base image vllm/vllm-openai:nightly-7794b1e08bf505ff28664515ffaaeeec955ab796,
vllm-project/vllm @ 7794b1e08bf5, 2026-08-05)

1. Tap the pre-norm AttnRes mixture as the Kimi K3 aux hidden state
   vllm/models/kimi_k3/nvidia/model.py
   vllm/envs.py
   Backport of https://github.com/vllm-project/vllm/pull/50487.

   Under AttnRes the tensor threaded between K3 layers is only the current
   block's running prefix sum; the blocks committed so far live separately in
   the block_residual bank. The old tap recorded ``prefix_sum +
   hidden_states``, i.e. a residual stream that no consumer in the model ever
   reads: both the next layer's attention front-end and the model's own
   output-side aggregation first run a softmax-weighted AttnRes mixture over
   ``bank[:num_blocks] + prefix``. That includes the last layer, whose logits
   come from ``attn_res(...)`` followed by the final norm, so the mismatch was
   not limited to the intermediate Eagle3 taps -- a drafter trained on the old
   capture was fit against features the verifier never sees.

Deviation from upstream: upstream ships VLLM_KIMI_K3_AUX_ATTN_RES_STREAM off
by default while the serving-side effect is measured. This image defaults it
on, since the pre-PR capture yields incorrect training targets and a silently
wrong default is the failure mode we care about here. Set
VLLM_KIMI_K3_AUX_ATTN_RES_STREAM=0 to reproduce upstream behaviour. The model
logs the active mode once at configuration time:
  Kimi-K3 aux hidden capture: layers=... mode=attn_res_stream
Once the base image carries PR #50487, drop this patch but keep exporting
VLLM_KIMI_K3_AUX_ATTN_RES_STREAM=1, or the default flips back to prefix_only.

Note: the v0.22.1 patch is not needed on this nightly:
- flash_attn rotary import fix: upstream, the import is now guarded with
  ``suppress(ModuleNotFoundError)`` in
  vllm/model_executor/layers/rotary_embedding/common.py

Apply:
  cd $VLLM_ROOT && git apply /path/to/vllm_k3.patch

